# Entry Main: `return: @` reached in code is refused by its missing operand (the book #return-in-data, #operand-storage; the
# grammar #close: the same receiver at body level is an internal return). The record is the one that describes a reference
# result in the data of a Structure; reached as the return of code, it is the operator @ without its operand. D describes
# `return: int`, so the return carries a result; the body of C writes node\seen, a field of D (node in C is D), then
# returns @. The call answers 2 and the effect stands: D\seen 1, r 0.
int: r 0
D:
    int: seen 0
    return: int
    C:
        node\seen := 1
        return: @
    end: C
end: D
---
Main:
    node\r := D\C()
